/**
 * The classroom sense of each word above — one short line, in the form a
 * six-year-old's ustazah would say it.
 *
 * "he created" rather than "created (3rd person masculine singular perfect)":
 * the gloss is read aloud to a child, so it is a sentence fragment they can
 * hear, and the past tense is kept because that is genuinely what the Arabic
 * form is. Passives are glossed as passives for the same reason — the whole
 * point of the خُلِقَ card is that the harakat changed who did the thing.
 */
